When a transition starts, Ladybird applies the element’s new style to
its layout node right away, which makes its anonymous descendants
inherit the transition’s start value. Blink’s LayoutBlock::
StyleDidChange() does the same, calling LayoutObject::
PropagateStyleToAnonymousChildren(). So does WebKit’s RenderBlock::
styleDidChange(), calling propagateStyleToAnonymousChildren() of its
RenderElement. And Gecko’s RestyleManager::ProcessPostTraversal()
calls nsIFrame::UpdateStyleOfOwnedAnonBoxes().
